# live_id50_913 — REAL fleet capture (id50 912→913, 2026-07-28), timeline /8.
# Payloads, orderings and retain flags are verbatim from the broker. TWO deliberate changes:
#   1. elapsed prefixes divided by 8 so the case runs in ~1 min instead of ~8;
#   2. `up=` divided by 8 TOO, because it is a DEVICE-reported duration that lives in the
#      payload and does not scale with the replay. Omitting this produced a false F=NO — the
#      auditor's own near-miss, and the reason rule 5 exists in this file's header.
# `tage=` is left unscaled: nothing here reads it, and changing more than necessary would cost
# the property that makes this fixture valuable — that the fleet, not us, produced the fields.
